answer.worked:
Complete the square and interchange $x$ and $y$.
$$\begin{align*}
y &= x^2-4x+6 \\
&= (x-2)^2+2 \\
x &= (y-2)^2+2 \\
x-2 &= (y-2)^2 \\
y-2 &= \sqrt{x-2}
\end{align*}$$
Since the original domain is $x\ge 2$, the inverse uses the positive square-root branch.
$$\begin{align*}
f^{-1}(x) &= 2+\sqrt{x-2}
\end{align*}$$

