answer.worked:
Let $y = -3x^2 - 1$ and restrict $x \geq 0$.
$$\begin{align*}
y &= -3x^2 - 1 \\
y + 1 &= -3x^2 \\
x^2 &= -\frac{y + 1}{3} \\
x &= \sqrt{-\frac{y + 1}{3}}
\end{align*}$$
Interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives:
$$\begin{align*}
y &= \sqrt{-\frac{x + 1}{3}}
\end{align*}$$
Therefore, $f^{-1}(x) = \sqrt{-\frac{x + 1}{3}}$.

